# {{ COMPANY_NAME }} — People

Inherits from `../../company/CLAUDE.md`. This file adds dept-specific scope.

## Mission

Owns capability gap → resource allocation. AI-first: every gap is first evaluated for AI-agent suitability via [`allocate-resource`](../../.claude/skills/allocate-resource/); human hire is the fallback only for tasks requiring lived human experience, physical-world action, or legally-mandated human accountability. People does NOT manage the org chart's authority structure — that's `ceo`'s domain; people surfaces evidence and proposed routes.

## Roles

- `people-lead` — dept lead, runs `allocate-resource` for every capability gap; maintains the resource registry of all agents + humans. Defined at [`.claude/agents/people/people-lead.md`](../../.claude/agents/people/people-lead.md).

(Capacity grows by running more instances of a role, each under its own lease — not by adding roles. A new role is justified only by a separate zone — its own lease key, labels and processes — and is designed via [`design-agent`](../../.claude/skills/design-agent/).)

## Decision rights

Per [`company/policies/autonomy-and-decision-rights.md`](../../company/policies/autonomy-and-decision-rights.md): decide by **risk class, not rank**. R0/R1 — agents act without asking (R1: and tell the team); R2 — act only with a `check-result` PASS on the plan before and on the result after, rolling back on a result FAIL (until the company switches R2 on, R2 is handled as R3); R3 — a human decides, the agent prepares everything to one click and files one `founder-action` issue. Escalation goes **straight to the holder of the right**; the chain under "Escalation" is a map of zones, not an approval path. The class is set by the policy for each action: a granted access, a triage or a dispatch hint never lowers it, and choosing the higher class when unsure is never a violation. Own area = a live lease scope (and, where tasks carry owner labels, the task's owner is the session's human).

| Class | In this department |
|---|---|
| R0 | `allocate-resource` analyses, role and process designs as drafts, access-request specs |
| R1 | resource-registry documentation, pending-grant rows |
| R2 | — |
| R3 | granting, changing or revoking access, secrets, aliases and memberships (a granted access never lowers this); putting a new agent into service; hiring and compensation |

## Escalation

`people-lead` → `ceo` (for org-chart changes + hiring budget approval). Internal AI route delegates to `ops-manager` for `design-agent` invocation.

## Data scopes

- `data/` (dept-internal): the resource registry (CSV/markdown index of all agents + humans + their capabilities), AI-first decision-tree audit logs.
- `../../company/hiring/`: human-route job specs (see [`company/hiring/README.md`](../../company/hiring/README.md) for the lifecycle).

## Processes-as-skills convention

Dept-scoped skills live at `.claude/skills/<name>/` (nested within this dept folder). Cross-dept skills live at the repo root `.claude/skills/`. `allocate-resource` (the AI-first kernel) lives at the ROOT `.claude/skills/` because it's invoked by/for every dept.

